.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-VAULT-CREATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-vault-create - Create a named ENV vault


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env vault create <vault> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a named vault in the active workspace. Its key is made on this computer and
wrapped with your ENV keys (and the team's, in a team workspace), so unlock them first
with pb env unlock. Names use lowercase letters, digits and -, up to 63 characters.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-vault(1)\fP
